/**
 * @file Modules.dox
 * @brief Doxygen module definitions. No code; this file exists only to give the generated
 *        navigation the same shape as the architecture.
 *
 * Grouped by layer rather than by folder, because the layering is the design: each group
 * depends only on the ones above it, and that acyclic order is what lets an algorithm be
 * written once and composed four ways. A flat, alphabetical file list would hide it.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup meta Meta
 * @brief Compile-time machinery: option packs, type lists, string literals as template
 *        parameters.
 *
 * Depends on nothing. `meta::OptionsPack` carries two kinds of entry -- flag tags matched by
 * type, and value options such as `patience<8>` read back with `get<K, Default>` -- and
 * `meta::AcceptsOnly` is what makes an unrecognised option a compile error rather than a
 * silently ignored one.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup util Utilities
 * @brief Bit twiddling, cache-line and inlining directives, thread registration, CPU topology.
 *
 * @ref util::threading::ThreadRegistry is the substantial one: a lock-free, unbounded registry
 * of per-thread state that both reclamation sources are built on. Everything else is small.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup core Core contracts
 * @brief Concepts only, no implementation.
 *
 * The contracts every other layer is written against: @ref core::Queue, @ref core::LinkedSegment,
 * @ref core::Proxy, @ref core::SegmentSource, @ref core::AdmissionPolicy, and
 * @ref core::segment_traits.
 *
 * `segment_traits` deliberately has **no primary definition**, so a segment that forgets to
 * declare its capabilities fails to compile rather than inheriting a default that happens to be
 * wrong. Note what concepts can and cannot say: they constrain *signatures*, not *obligations* --
 * "has an `enqueue(T, bool)`" is checkable, "refuses permanently once full" is not. Obligations
 * are written down in @ref extending and enforced by SegmentLifecycleTest.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup mem Memory
 * @brief Single-block co-allocation, handle types, and the reclamation sources.
 *
 * A segment is one allocation: header and cell array in the same block, laid out by
 * @ref mem::LayoutBuilder and reached through @ref mem::SingleBlock. A source
 * (@ref mem::source::Hazard, @ref mem::source::Pool) decides where segments come from and when
 * they may be reused, and carries the proxy's per-thread state alongside its own.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup cell Cells and tagging
 * @brief How one slot is laid out, and how a word encodes empty / consumed / claimed / payload.
 *
 * Three segments previously hand-rolled three incompatible encodings for the same problem, two
 * of which spelled "reserved" the same way and meant different things. @ref cell::Tagging states
 * the contract positively instead, in terms of what a word *is*.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup linkage Linkage
 * @brief Whether an algorithm carries a successor handle.
 *
 * @ref linkage::None is an empty struct, so under `[[no_unique_address]]` a standalone queue
 * pays nothing for being linkable -- measurably: `sizeof(queue::Vyukov<T*>)` is 384 bytes
 * against 512 for `seg::Vyukov<T*>`, exactly one padded next-pointer apart.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup algo Algorithms
 * @brief The queue algorithms themselves, each written once and parameterised by linkage.
 *
 * Bounded rings usable standalone (`queue::`) or as a linked segment (`seg::`), plus two index
 * containers -- @ref algo::PhasedBucket and @ref algo::CacheRing -- that exist to serve the
 * pooled source's epoch rotation rather than to hold user payloads.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup proxy Proxies
 * @brief Composing segments into an unbounded or bounded queue.
 *
 * One traversal, @ref proxy::LinkedProxy, over three policy axes: what stops admission, where
 * segments come from, and which algorithm is inside each. This replaced four near-identical
 * proxies that had each re-implemented the same Michael-Scott traversal.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup registry Registry
 * @brief The single place that declares which implementations exist.
 *
 * One `Entry<"name", Type>` line reaches the benchmark's `--list`, the typed conformance suite
 * and the concurrency matrix at once. Selection by name is a compile-time fold, so the measured
 * loop stays monomorphic -- no vtable, no `std::function`, no variant.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup tests Tests
 * @brief What each suite pins down.
 *
 * See @ref testing for how to run them, the four build configurations, and the isolation-harness
 * technique used to find the concurrency bugs.
 */
